body:
Fixes #326607

### Problem

When a Markdown table is activated for editing, the theme renders the source pipes and the delimiter row (`| --- |`) in place of the cell borders. In a narrow editor pane the automatic table layout kept compressing the columns until those rendered pipes and dashes overlapped the cell text, and the delimiter row wrapped onto a second line.

### Fix

Hold an active table at its content width and let its wrapper scroll horizontally instead of crushing the columns:

```css
.md-theme-vscode-default .md-table-wrapper {
	overflow-x: auto;
}

.md-theme-vscode-default .md-table.md-block-active {
	width: max-content;
}
```

`width: max-content` on the active table is what stops the compression that caused the overlap, so no extra per row rule is needed. Both rules are scoped to `.md-theme-vscode-default` to match the existing theme rules and to keep the width override above `.md-theme-vscode-default .md-table` in specificity.

### Verification

Captured from a live Code - OSS build of this branch.

Editing mode in a narrow pane with the chat side bar open. The table scrolls horizontally and the pipes stay aligned with the cell text:

![Narrow editing pane, table aligned and horizontally scrollable](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/myselfsiddharth/vscode/assets/326607-screenshots/04-live-code-oss.png)

After hiding the secondary side bar. The full table fits and the closing pipes line up on the right gridline:

![Wider pane, full table fits with aligned borders](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/myselfsiddharth/vscode/assets/326607-screenshots/05-live-narrow-fixed.png)
